<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Honduras.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Honduras</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tiburcio Carías Andino begins sixteen years of rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/nazi-germany"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazi%20Germany.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazi Germany</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hitler is appointed chancellor; the Enabling Act lets his cabinet make laws without parliament</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mari"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mari.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mari</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bedouin find a statue on Tell Hariri, leading to French excavations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mapungubwe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Mapungubwe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Mapungubwe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The University of Pretoria begins excavations on Mapungubwe Hill</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/dictatorship"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dictatorship.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dictatorship</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Adolf Hitler becomes chancellor; the Enabling Act lets his cabinet make laws without the Reichstag</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/one-party-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/One-party%20state.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>One-party state</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany’s Law against the Formation of New Parties makes the Nazi Party the only legal party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/parliamentary-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Parliamentary%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Parliamentary democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Reichstag passes the Enabling Act, ending parliamentary government in the Weimar Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/oriental-republic-of-uruguay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Oriental%20Republic%20of%20Uruguay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Oriental Republic of Uruguay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gabriel Terra dissolves the General Assembly in a coup and governs by decree; a new constitution of 1934 strengthens the presidency.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/manchukuo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manchukuo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manchukuo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The League of Nations endorses the Lytton Report in February, finding Japan had broken international law; Japan withdraws from the League.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-cuba-1902-1959"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Cuba%20(1902-1959).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Cuba (1902-1959)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A general strike, sugar workers' uprisings and an army revolt force Gerardo Machado into exile; in September the Sergeants' Revolt under Fulgencio Batista overthrows his successor.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/navajo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Navajo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Navajo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The federal government begins the Navajo Livestock Reduction, made mandatory in 1935</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/bauhaus"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bauhaus.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bauhaus</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the Gestapo shuts the Berlin school, Mies and the faculty agree to close it themselves</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/fascism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fascism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fascism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Nazi Party under Adolf Hitler takes power in Germany, and liberal democracy there is dissolved</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-state-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20State%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free State of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Göring becomes Prussian minister president, and the Landtag meets for the last time on 18 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tibet-1912-1951"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tibet%20(1912-1951).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tibet (1912-1951)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 13th Dalai Lama died, and China sent a condolence mission to Lhasa headed by General Huang Musong</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/weimar-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Weimar%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Weimar Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Reichstag passes the Enabling Act, ending the republic in effect</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/second-spanish-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Spanish%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Spanish Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Spanish Confederation of the Autonomous Right (CEDA) wins the elections, opening the &quot;black biennium&quot;</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/albert-einstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Albert%20Einstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Albert Einstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Surrenders his passport in Antwerp after the Nazis take power, and in October takes up a post at the Institute for Advanced Study</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/temperance-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Temperance%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Temperance movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Twenty-first Amendment is ratified on 5 December and repeals nationwide prohibition</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/nazism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hitler is appointed Chancellor in January; the Reichstag Fire Decree and the Enabling Act follow, and the Nazis establish a one-party state</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/christian-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Christian%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Christian democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Centre Party and the Christian Social People's Service sign the Enabling Act after the Nazis take power, and both then dissolve</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/jehovahs-witnesses"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jehovah's%20Witnesses.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jehovah's Witnesses</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">About 20,000 Witnesses live in Nazi Germany, and about 10,000 of them are imprisoned over the following years</span></li></ul></section>
